# Cell from playpick: mode=daily, boss=gift, spec=warrior:arms, style=mash,
# view=844x390,touch, save=carried.
#
# Probe (open + tap daily) showed the daily screen itself: today's actual run
# is "The Two Flasks", 25-player normal, SWARMING -- not "gift". playpick's
# `boss` axis for mode=daily is drawn from ENCOUNTERS the same way it is for
# mode=raid (scripts/playpick.ts line 116), but a daily's boss is picked by
# the date (src/sim/daily.ts dailyFor(), keyed off dailyKey()), never by the
# player -- there is no control on this screen that could ever make "gift"
# come up. Playing the cell as assigned is therefore impossible; playing
# whatever the daily actually is, honestly, is the only option. Worth writing
# into direction.md as a driver-tooling note once this session is done.
#
# What is new here regardless of boss: first warrior:arms this job has ever
# played (warrior:protection has, arms has not -- class:1 on the daily grid,
# confirmed against src/sim/classes.ts's spec list), and the first mash-style
# pull of any daily. The Two Flasks was played once before (2026-09-24,
# paladin protection, dodge, carried) and wiped at 152s/24% boss blaming
# `caustic` at 95.5 hits/min -- direction.md flagged that as worth a second
# data point under a different style before trusting it as its own complaint.
# This is that second point.
